#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096350 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "12811582-7156-5b84-9ba9-5545f87894f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3993" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "c7373a16-c90a-5875-8b17-8724542b35ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-493" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "672d52f6-89d8-550d-863b-7c5157d59ca3" :question/math-academy-id "e-494" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c8a9b38-30a3-52b1-9fff-2a4d191e1c43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300057} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0aee70-f173-5908-827f-5f89cb4c0afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300058} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8e01d5-889e-5b4a-9acb-3c0c035897a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300059} {:answer/id #uuid "736ab1b5-d37e-536f-886c-19bb16961a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300060} {:answer/id #uuid "d3877c7f-5c76-5950-9f56-cf76e73251f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3877c7f-5c76-5950-9f56-cf76e73251f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300061} :answer-field/id #uuid "12cfabff-92bf-56e2-9172-fe6f118c2de8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e6583e6-92e6-5c07-b4f7-1730072676de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114553" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0aef57-abe2-5e9b-8ffd-b4ac250e8856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300085} {:answer/id #uuid "9fec5b92-742f-5131-b6ee-8697e0573919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300086} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4d5c0b-b085-55f3-bba7-69a470201edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300087} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf8ad37-97c5-52c4-9f50-a7d3b497740a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300088} {:answer/id #uuid "260a2b08-273c-5530-b4b4-c3d9f234169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "260a2b08-273c-5530-b4b4-c3d9f234169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300089} :answer-field/id #uuid "507e7950-22fa-5522-8d6e-e608954b5950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df4a8ff9-b6f1-509e-8da7-ab67f79ced45" :question/math-academy-id "q-114579" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13464e63-1657-559d-8a28-699cd51ad462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301512} {:answer/id #uuid "7edc9cc9-d471-528e-8546-4a59b2f203d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301513} {:answer/id #uuid "56cfb89d-737e-5b4b-b164-bd69bc88630e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301514} {:answer/id #uuid "47263fdf-3252-5758-901c-ebc791afddc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301515} {:answer/id #uuid "392bd0fa-9952-5802-bd29-97ab9c658a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "392bd0fa-9952-5802-bd29-97ab9c658a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301516} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7f656bc-8a9e-57c4-9968-b809486d5ebf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acfabbf7-741d-5b7a-a2d2-0388e3cd4c2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12566" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡(x))(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b5a0e89-dafd-5cc0-8d77-5825f7d7a8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2\\ln 2}(x\\ln (3x) - 2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094263} {:answer/id #uuid "b22a5f14-2bcb-5e6f-9b5b-23b0cb3679f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2\\ln 2}(\\ln (3x) + 2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094264} {:answer/id #uuid "0afcda7f-e8df-5f02-bfd8-f61b328a5df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4\\ln 2}(2\\ln (3x) + 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094265} {:answer/id #uuid "61eae961-7622-535b-86c2-5784657a92b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2\\ln 2}(\\ln (3x) - 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094266} {:answer/id #uuid "722ad2f9-d257-58ec-b5b0-c1ff021aa62c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4\\ln 2}(2\\ln (3x) - 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "722ad2f9-d257-58ec-b5b0-c1ff021aa62c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4\\ln 2}(2\\ln (3x) - 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094267} :answer-field/id #uuid "d122cc31-d5fe-52a8-9d44-e81189e6199a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8f0b656-4bc9-55ad-bafd-83e444f61957" :question/math-academy-id "q-12568" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(3x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058af3d2-4de9-51f1-b45e-c4f6450388df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300106} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb1ad74-0ddf-591a-a83b-388cef01dd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300107} {:answer/id #uuid "d79fb862-748b-5e76-ab02-bc440f18ad12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300108} {:answer/id #uuid "caaad1f2-f17b-50eb-b0e1-dddf4b14cf61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{x}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300109} {:answer/id #uuid "af3459a1-862b-5808-a104-ece7d60650b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cb1ad74-0ddf-591a-a83b-388cef01dd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300107} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0d112d-a83b-571f-8593-0c01ad5a42de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "252da65e-a015-52db-8aca-5c1050a5b779" :question/math-academy-id "q-12573" :question/problem "$\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int (x+7)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x-7\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74057c0f-e278-5c96-b2b6-269573b365d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301519} {:answer/id #uuid "a98dec41-c185-511f-b86f-d11d62686a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301520} {:answer/id #uuid "666ecd74-b3c3-5da0-b19b-17cfa47eb155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301521} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7634a5-e2ae-58f4-a3b4-b804a8f06673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301522} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf15308-86cc-55ce-ada5-5f70383b7ec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74057c0f-e278-5c96-b2b6-269573b365d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301519} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf19432a-bda6-5cce-bcb9-aa042d58eb7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc69208e-918d-5ad0-916e-0a8f50777de1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14722" :question/problem "$\\int 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot {x}^{2}-\\int {x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-2\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c9d3037-4fbf-5129-8a62-c161025d5a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-6x\\sqrt{x}-4\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301526} {:answer/id #uuid "91698760-bd12-5999-9fef-4df6573b0163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301527} {:answer/id #uuid "e9728da4-774b-503d-b729-29a92e198f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}-6\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301528} {:answer/id #uuid "ad30295d-1136-5e50-b7a0-fda7459d537c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+6x\\sqrt{x}-4\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301529} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9a36eb-5254-53fc-bbb1-dfe11f1ec5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4x\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91698760-bd12-5999-9fef-4df6573b0163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301527} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fcc91ad-2d4b-5a3b-bbe1-275d7b8a9f1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1cbc4f3-c36a-51f9-819b-9221ea4ff42b" :question/math-academy-id "q-2429" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(2\\sqrt{x})-\\int (2\\sqrt{x})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-4\\sqrt{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "239eed72-3016-52bd-9509-b0b5ff978706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "239eed72-3016-52bd-9509-b0b5ff978706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301533} :answer-field/id #uuid "5578b927-5d8c-5e1d-9eaa-a72aab5a6f04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12fdbac6-b0fe-5529-b377-32ed7d4fe6fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-350960" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad9ad490-8d79-549f-9c25-d17ebabe1e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{52e^{14}+4}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad9ad490-8d79-549f-9c25-d17ebabe1e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{52e^{14}+4}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301536} :answer-field/id #uuid "836698fc-7f29-5146-8d66-1ef9cfde66fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b7a04644-a966-560d-8fe0-a0cecdf92a78" :question/math-academy-id "q-350965" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{6} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{6}\\,dx=\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{4({e}^{2})^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4(1)^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{7}]-\\frac{4}{7}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{14}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{49}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{14}}{7}-(\\frac{4{e}^{14}}{49}-\\frac{4}{49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}(56{e}^{14}-4{e}^{14}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{49}(13{e}^{14}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa99a0c-c5b5-5a52-826d-f3dae4a9214d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301539} {:answer/id #uuid "1c788a7c-739c-564f-ac07-de204c9ffd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c788a7c-739c-564f-ac07-de204c9ffd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301540} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8f8f17b-26a1-5931-9b5e-85d1dfd9ddd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01434e96-0acb-5606-b679-13b67a626150" :question/math-academy-id "q-350967" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,(x){|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{e}{2})\\,(\\frac{e}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\,(\\frac{1}{2})]-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/2}^{e/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}e-\\frac{1}{2}e+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2426fed9-5fc5-557f-b1eb-a34eac694e16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301543} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5e2c14-c39c-5342-aaba-87dcb319f28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301544} {:answer/id #uuid "af98e46c-fa9d-5313-b126-992f4053f0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301545} {:answer/id #uuid "eb88b6a5-3216-59c8-9dbd-dcc8cd9b01fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301546} {:answer/id #uuid "47831ab8-c986-503f-9bc9-e4829f3b72e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af98e46c-fa9d-5313-b126-992f4053f0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301545} :answer-field/id #uuid "39cd5324-1290-5fd0-a5e1-c982fa76ad28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a679d6ab-62b1-5316-b84d-9712f4ecec56" :question/math-academy-id "q-49712" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(x){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e-x{|}_{1}^{e}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}(e-e+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03ab38cf-a5af-5384-bdb0-adebedb61c03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293944} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0342b1-2889-533a-b143-2aaa9b3865da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293945} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc97104-c440-566b-8fdd-51084aa09457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293946} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ba874e-8dcf-5530-8e52-ba8a0c690296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293947} {:answer/id #uuid "61a7f51c-b809-5293-9060-2e7e447669a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61a7f51c-b809-5293-9060-2e7e447669a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293948} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e49af5d-d2fe-5544-93ff-5bc43178ebe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0002bb48-63e3-5869-82b8-396b34ff4061" :question/math-academy-id "q-78962" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac331f0a-166a-5ba1-ad0b-005ba063d432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301550} {:answer/id #uuid "be892953-b28f-5d13-9a66-bc3a59502428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301551} {:answer/id #uuid "882702ef-d805-51f1-a920-8e3e9c05415d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301552} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4f4c04-f28d-5a23-9a3e-be8dc893989e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301553} {:answer/id #uuid "54c3dacc-1766-5d5d-b7f0-9c564b552007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb4f4c04-f28d-5a23-9a3e-be8dc893989e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301553} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa6a480-20a5-52af-bb4a-fe3c74b08122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b9ed7c7-8416-5dd4-8ed9-af068b0cd0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-78963" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 9{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\cdot (3{x}^{3})-\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d354ac99-1e1b-53ee-b795-8711beff0f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301557} {:answer/id #uuid "56c909fb-acbb-567b-abe4-5c75e7690427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301558} {:answer/id #uuid "96ddcca3-5d15-53aa-8370-73a73f650fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301559} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd447bf-6974-56de-9e1a-45f92ecd766c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301560} {:answer/id #uuid "f3649b73-f7da-5804-a676-ae738e75bb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d354ac99-1e1b-53ee-b795-8711beff0f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301557} :answer-field/id #uuid "56fe89b8-1b85-5f44-841a-cf5b2ec294dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ece8a685-6392-5fbc-8337-860c17b91242" :question/math-academy-id "q-78966" :question/problem "$\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8803e90-c191-52d6-8000-b1786a6f2b98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293951} {:answer/id #uuid "c33681d6-952b-5538-8d83-59c7b03cbb1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293952} {:answer/id #uuid "93bad77f-fc4c-5151-b61a-1e3552e61d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293953} {:answer/id #uuid "24b67811-2588-5ef9-b110-04869e9d624f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293954} {:answer/id #uuid "0b28fab3-cd5e-5936-b51e-8b0a7c76cac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93bad77f-fc4c-5151-b61a-1e3552e61d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293953} :answer-field/id #uuid "69fc184d-93d8-5619-91bc-9ecb7ce71f48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f8b4061-8471-5977-a76a-c60012c56f62" :question/math-academy-id "q-78973" :question/problem "$\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-2x+C \\\\  & =2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}]}
